{"title":"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 27","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the adjoining figure, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is a diameter of the circle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> is a chord parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, \nand <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54dcbaf9d32502609180e24afdd5498061998616.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AED = \\alpha$\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" />. The ratio of the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/8/b984c55719cc5f992ee62656d920ac15c78d9137.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> to that of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/5/9057d4d264f5530ac63d366089bc3c17ce5d79a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is  \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/8/5287124b7c64cb0da4d33b2a32c979894f04d5d7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] defaultpen(fontsize(10pt)+linewidth(.8pt)); pair A=(-1,0), B=(1,0), E=(0,-.4), C=(.6,-.8), D=(-.6,-.8), E=(0,-.8/(1.6)); draw(unitcircle); draw(A--B--D--C--A); draw(Arc(E,.2,155,205)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,W); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,C); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,C); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,W); label(&quot;$\\alpha$&quot;,E-(.2,0),W); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,E,N); [/asy]\" width=\"668\" height=\"632\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/8/6682b4c3d11d34e688bb0196cff4f2c8023f9237.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\cos\\ \\alpha\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\sin\\ \\alpha\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\cos^2\\alpha\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\sin^2\\alpha\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 1-\\sin\\ \\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"567\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><br />  \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/8/fd85454c0ce4000c0e63b4a1c4a12ef6f8b56e9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/8/5b8451bee5a68657a8f8d5c57de669c2de023c04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DCE$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> are similar isosceles triangles. It remains to find the square of the ratio of their sides. Draw in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is a diameter, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/7/8b7cb65211ae878cd8565ab1a979576cbba3db20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ADB=\\angle ADE=90^{\\circ}$\" width=\"185\" height=\"13\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/9/ec94346de7816a6e8d4ebb4cfb038c6a5575bf42.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{DE}{AE}=\\cos\\alpha\\]\" width=\"94\" height=\"37\" /> So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/109020d930f188ac7d6b98d14416890eb0375715.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{DE^2}{AE^2}=\\cos^2\\alpha\\]\" width=\"109\" height=\"39\" /> The answer is thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/2/dc233d3e097d83bdeb1caed0fe6a06b90b8195dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"36\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME\" title=\"1986 AHSME\">1986 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1986 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1986\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 26\">Problem 26</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 28\">Problem 28</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"